## Verun Solana MVP — environment
##
## DO NOT commit real secrets to this file. It is checked into git as a
## template only. Real keys live in `.env` (gitignored) on each developer
## machine and in Vercel project env vars in production.
##
## To populate your local `.env`:
##   1) cp .env.example .env
##   2) npm run genkey   (generates a fresh Devnet keypair + airdrops 1 SOL)
##   3) Paste the printed SOLANA_PUBLIC + SOLANA_SECRET (b58) values into .env
##
## Or paste an existing keypair you control.

# Required: signer secret key. Two formats accepted:
#   1) base58 string (~88 chars)
#   2) JSON array of 64 bytes — the format `solana-keygen new` writes
SOLANA_SECRET=PASTE_BASE58_SECRET_HERE

# Public address of the signer. Optional — derived from SOLANA_SECRET if missing.
# If set, /api/config-check verifies it matches the secret.
SOLANA_PUBLIC=PASTE_BASE58_PUBKEY_HERE

# Solana RPC endpoint (Devnet by default).
# For higher rate limits / reliable airdrops, switch to a paid RPC
# (Helius, Triton, QuickNode) and paste the URL here.
SOLANA_RPC=https://api.devnet.solana.com

# Cluster name used in explorer URLs ("devnet" / "testnet" / "mainnet-beta").
SOLANA_CLUSTER=devnet

# How many recent signatures to scan for the SBT registry.
SBT_SCAN_LIMIT=200

# Local express port (only for `npm run api`, not Vercel).
PORT=3010
